ftrace: drop weak function locations of modules when loading them

Lawrence Lin's v2 series of 2026-10-04, both patches, as posted to the
trace and modules lists, where it waits on Steven Rostedt; carried here
until the kernel has it.

Since b39181f7c690 ("ftrace: Add FTRACE_MCOUNT_MAX_OFFSET to avoid
adding weak function"), ftrace_module_enable() calls test_for_valid_rec()
for every ftrace record of a module as it loads, and for a module's
address kallsyms_lookup() walks the module's whole symbol table. A load
costs records times symbols, under ftrace_lock. On this laptop amdgpu
formed at 1.9 s but reached its first notifier only at 7.0 s, and
btintel's load waited on the lock behind it for 4.7 s. Boots with no
probes start amdgpu as late, so the desk's monitor stays dark that long.

The series sorts the module's symbol addresses once and marks each
location that lies at most FTRACE_MCOUNT_MAX_OFFSET after one, zeroing
the rest before they become records, as sorttable does for vmlinux.

